The hostname or IP address of the door repository server.
# RepoHost=bbs.uprough.net

The TCP port number for the repository server connection. Valid range: 1-65535.
If an invalid value is specified, the default is used.
# RepoPort=80

The HTTP path prefix for the repository API endpoints.
# RepoPath=/api/door-repo

The AmigaDOS directory where downloaded door archives are saved. Must exist
before use. This door will not create the directory automatically. The
install index (DoorRepo.idx, one line per installed door) is kept here too.
# DownloadDir=T:

The number of doors to display per page when browsing the repository.
Valid range: 1-9999. If an invalid value is specified, the default is used.
# PageSize=20

The maximum number of seconds to wait for a response from the repository server.
Valid range: 1-3600 (1 second to 1 hour). If an invalid value is specified,
the default is used.
# TimeoutSecs=30

The AmigaDOS directory an installed door's files are put in. The BBS
command name chosen at install time is appended to it, so a door installed
as MYDOOR lands in Doors/MYDOOR/. Must exist before use.
# DoorsDir=Doors/

The AmigaDOS directory holding BBS command configs. Installing writes
<CMD>.info here; uninstalling removes it. Must exist before use.
# BBSCmdDir=BBSCmd/

The name or full path of the LHA archive extraction utility, used by
[I]nstall and if ExtractAfterDownload is enabled.
# LhaCommand=lha

Whether to automatically extract downloaded archives after downloading them.
Accepts: yes, no, 1, or 0. Any other value defaults to no (0).
# ExtractAfterDownload=no

Whether to keep a downloaded archive whose checksum did not match, renamed
to <name>.bad, instead of deleting it. Accepts: yes, no, 1, or 0. Default is
no. Turn it on only while investigating a mismatch: the digest tells you the
bytes were wrong, the file is the only thing that can tell you how. Any
previous .bad for the same archive is replaced, so this cannot accumulate.
# KeepFailedDownloads=no

Whether to use the full-screen ANSI browser. Accepts: yes, no, 1, or 0.
Default is yes. Set it to no on a terminal that cannot handle CSI escape
sequences; the door then falls back to the original line-at-a-time listing,
which needs nothing but plain text.
# Ansi=yes

Terminal geometry for the full-screen browser. Ignored when Ansi=no.
Defaults are the universal BBS 80x24; raise them if your users connect on a
larger window. Valid ranges: ScreenRows 10-200, ScreenCols 40-250.
# ScreenRows=24
# ScreenCols=80

The AmigaDOS path where the door logs its activity and errors.
# LogFile=T:DoorRepo.log

CONFIGURATION NOTES
---

This file is optional. If it does not exist or is empty, all settings default
to the values shown above.

Key names are case-insensitive: RepoHost, repohost, and REPOHOST all work.

Leading and trailing whitespace around key names and values is automatically
trimmed. For example, these are all equivalent:
  RepoHost=example.com
  RepoHost = example.com
  RepoHost   =   example.com

Comments start with the number sign (#) and extend to the end of the line.
Blank lines are ignored.

If a value is invalid (non-numeric, out of range, or unrecognized), the line
is silently skipped and that setting retains its default value. Invalid values
do not stop the door from starting; they are logged (if LogFile is writable)
and the door continues with the default configuration.

EXAMPLE CONFIGURATIONS
---

Conservative settings for slow networks:
RepoHost=bbs.example.net
RepoPort=80
TimeoutSecs=60
PageSize=10

Aggressive settings for fast networks:
RepoHost=bbs.example.net
RepoPort=8080
TimeoutSecs=10
PageSize=50

Extract downloads automatically to RAM for faster access:
ExtractAfterDownload=yes
DownloadDir=RAM:
LhaCommand=7z
